    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on speed and high-leverage plate appearances, anchored by our two lead-off hitters. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Christian Yelich** (74.67) represent our strongest plays today, both benefiting from ideal matchups against favorable right-handed arms in Feltner and Cecconi. Their shared advantage isn't just the batting order; both earn a boost from slow opposing deliveries, creating prime environments for stolen base production\u2014a category we are prioritizing aggressively. **Kyle Schwarber** (69.09) and **Carson Benge** (67.04) round out our top tier, with **Kyle Schwarber**\u2019s elite 0.388 xwOBA and **Carson Benge**\u2019s advantageous lead-off spot against Singer providing significant run-production upside that outweighs the risks of their respective park factors.\n\nWhile the top of the order carries the day, our bench decision came down to a razor-thin margin between **Chase Meidroth** and **Caleb Durbin**. Ultimately, **Caleb Durbin** (44.93) fell just shy of the active roster; despite a positive park factor, his output was suppressed by an unfavorable matchup against Cease, whose elite 3.07 xERA severely limits the ceiling for our utility hitters. We opted to stay with **Chase Meidroth** (50.64) for the slightly more favorable matchup against Cole. We are monitoring **Junior Caminero** (59.92) closely; despite his strong projection, he faces a tough lefty in Wrobleski, and we are managing his exposure carefully to maintain our game cap efficiency. The rest of the bench, including **Dillon Dingler** (34.06), remains below the Zebras' 40-point floor for starting consideration today, keeping the lineup lean and focused on maximizing high-efficiency outcomes.",
